==============================================================================
Separate-process components (not included, not linked)
==============================================================================

The Compose files and Helm charts run these servers from their upstream
images as separate processes. They are not part of this source or of the
VegaDūta images, and each is licensed under its own terms.

Default components:

  - PostgreSQL (PostgreSQL License), with pgvector (PostgreSQL License) and
    Apache AGE (Apache-2.0), built into the postgres image from their
    upstream sources by deploy/postgres/Dockerfile
  - Valkey (BSD-3-Clause)          cache and rate limiting
  - Keycloak (Apache-2.0)          identity provider
  - SeaweedFS (Apache-2.0)         S3-compatible object storage (Full tier)
  - PgBouncer (ISC)                connection pooling (Full tier)

Optional, by Compose profile:

  - Redpanda (Business Source License 1.1)          `events`, `temporal`, `jobs`
  - Temporal server and UI (MIT)                    `temporal`, `jobs`
  - Grafana, Loki, Promtail (AGPL-3.0)              `observability`
  - Prometheus (Apache-2.0), redis_exporter (MIT)   `observability`
  - Langfuse (MIT; its image also contains separately licensed enterprise
    code that stays inactive without a license key), ClickHouse (Apache-2.0)
                                                    `tracing`
  - FreeLLMAPI (MIT)                                `freellmapi`
  - Hindsight (MIT)                                 `hindsight`
  - LiveKit server (Apache-2.0)                     `voice`
  - SearXNG (AGPL-3.0)                              `search`
                                         (deploy/compose/docker-compose.search.yml)

Replaceable alternatives mentioned in the docs:

  - MinIO (AGPL-3.0): any S3-compatible object store works; SeaweedFS is the
    default.
  - Redis 7.4+ (RSALv2/SSPLv1): Valkey is the default and a drop-in
    replacement.
